'''[[Sanyan]]''' is a sovereign island city-state archipelago located west of [[Ayorin]] on the [[Kaftia]]n mainland. The nation is defined by its use of the ancient Kinza script and the Kojoda calendar, as well as its adherence to the traditional Orisa-Ifa religion. Since the discovery of petroleum in 1896 and the nationalization of the industry in 1921 following the [[Baliscan Revolution]], Sanyan has grown into one of the world's leading oil producers and exporters.

As a high-income economy, Sanyan is noted for its high Human Development Index, offering universal healthcare and tuition-free university education with no personal income tax. It maintains a significant international presence as a middle power, exerting cultural and political influence across the Kaftian diaspora through the Noya media group and its advocacy for Pan-Kaftianism. The state is a founding member of the Kaftian Union and the Concepcion Organization of Cooperation.

